        "original_id": "c0715ae6-6bf8-5a24-8336-e76fdd1d1072",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Liliʻuokalani\n- Works: “Aloha ʻOe”\n- Places: Hawaii, Kingdom of Hawaii\n\nFacts:\n- Liliʻuokalani was born as Lydia Liliʻu Loloku Walania Wewehi Kamakaʻeha on September 2, 1838.\n- Liliʻuokalani was the last monarch of the Kingdom of Hawaii.\n- Liliʻuokalani ruled the Kingdom of Hawaii from January 29, 1891 until the overthrow of the kingdom on January 17, 1893.\n- “Aloha ʻOe” (“Farewell to Thee”) is Liliʻuokalani’s most famous song.\n- “Aloha ʻOe” is a common cultural symbol for Hawaii.\n- Liliʻuokalani died on November 11, 1917.",
